{
  // WARP-329 class — `vitest` does not typecheck (esbuild strips types), and
  // `tsconfig.json` excludes `__tests__`, so until this file existed NOT ONE
  // of the 133 tests under `__tests__/` was ever seen by `tsc`: not by a bare
  // `npx tsc` in the package, and not by `ship-check.sh tsc-full` (its phase 3
  // runs each workspace's own tsconfig). PR #261 shipped a TS2322 in a test
  // fixture through exactly this hole.
  //
  // It deliberately `extends` the package config rather than redeclaring the
  // module settings, so tests are checked under the SAME flags the package
  // actually builds with (`module: NodeNext` + no `"type": "module"` in
  // package.json = CommonJS output). That is the whole point: relaxing
  // `module` here to make `import.meta` legal would hide the TS1470 class this
  // check exists to catch, and would put tools-core on the opposite convention
  // from `apps/orchestrator`, whose tests live under `src/` and are already
  // checked as CJS (see the note at
  // `apps/orchestrator/src/__tests__/write-tools-derivation.guard.test.ts:25-28`).
  //
  // Only the two keys below are overridden:
  //   - `noEmit`  — this is a check, not a build; `tsconfig.json` still owns
  //                 the emit that produces `dist/`.
  //   - `rootDir` — widened from `./src` to `.` so `__tests__/` is not
  //                 reported as TS6059 "not under rootDir".
  //
  // `declaration: true` is inherited and deliberately NOT overridden: it is a
  // no-op under `noEmit`, and TypeScript has allowed the pair since 5.0
  // (verified on the lockfile-pinned 5.9.3 — the combination raises nothing).
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": "."
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*", "__tests__/**/*"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
